而且我觉得它很真实的一点是，你知道的，他们去酒吧可能是因为那里有免费的食物和免费的饮料，你知道的，他们手头很紧，我觉得这群人。

00:08:22.894 --> 00:08:30.954
Yeah, they're on a, they're on a budget, nobody's rich except maybe Barney, but you don't even really know what he does or whether it's all talk.
对，他们手头很紧，没有人是有钱人，除了巴尼可能算，但你甚至不知道他是干什么的，或者他是不是在吹牛。

00:08:30.954 --> 00:08:33.622
But yeah, Marshall, Marshall is in a tight spot.
不过说真的，马歇尔，马歇尔处境艰难。

00:08:33.622 --> 00:08:37.958
He's, yeah, he's already being seduced by this huge salary he's being offered.
他，是的，他已经开始被提供的高薪给诱惑了。

00:08:37.958 --> 00:08:48.409
And he doesn't even know the part where they're massively in debt and we're not going to find that out until the next episode where I can see Marshall find that out until the next episode.
而且他还不知道他们背负巨额债务的事，直到下一集我们才会看到马歇尔发现这件事。

00:08:48.409 --> 00:08:49.909
I like the tension of that.
我很喜欢这种紧张感。

00:08:49.909 --> 00:09:01.290
It really is like, I think as a writer, what a thing like to always ask yourself and as early as you can is like, what is their relationship to money?
这真的很像，作为一个编剧，你脑海里总要问自己、而且要尽早问自己的一个问题是：他们和钱的关系是什么？

00:09:01.290 --> 00:09:04.400
What is their relationship to their work?
他们和工作关系是什么？

00:09:04.400 --> 00:09:07.890
Who are they in the world vis-a-vis resources?
站在资源的立场上，他们在世界上的定位是谁？

00:09:07.890 --> 00:09:10.470
And I love that you guys did this.
我很高兴你们这样处理了。

00:09:10.470 --> 00:09:17.350
And I think that also, you set up a great, great ethical dilemma for Marshall.
而且我认为，你们也为马歇尔设定了一个非常、非常棒的道德困境。

00:09:17.590 --> 00:09:18.090
Yeah.
对。

00:09:18.090 --> 00:09:18.590
Yeah.
对。

00:09:18.590 --> 00:09:22.077
And he really, really seems sink into the quicksand of that dilemma.
而且他真的、真的仿佛陷入了那个困境的流沙之中。

00:09:21.590 --> 00:09:23.481
And it's a very real dilemma.
这是一个非常现实的困境。

00:09:23.481 --> 00:09:26.350
Everyone's been in that dilemma where he is.
每个人都经历过他所处的这种困境。

00:09:26.350 --> 00:09:28.111
He wants to have four kids.
他想要四个孩子。

00:09:28.111 --> 00:09:35.220
Lily wants to, not four, but he really wants to make a living, but he also really wants to save planet Earth.
莉莉想要，虽然不是四个，但他真的很想维持生计，但他同时也真的很想拯救地球。

00:09:35.220 --> 00:09:36.198
And it's great.
这太棒了。

00:09:36.198 --> 00:09:39.590
It's great to see him torn between those two things.
看到他在这两者之间挣扎非常精彩。

00:09:39.590 --> 00:09:45.490
And I really liked the idea and the Simpsons occasionally did this with Marge Simpson, which I also loved.
我很喜欢这个构思——《辛普森一家》偶尔也会在玛姬·辛普森身上这样做，我也很喜欢。

00:09:45.490 --> 00:09:47.939
We really made Lily not the voice of reason.
我们真的没有把莉莉塑造成纯粹的理性之声。

00:09:47.939 --> 00:09:51.112
Lily often has to be the voice of like, here's what's up.
莉莉通常扮演的是那种“情况是这样的”的角色。

00:09:51.112 --> 00:09:54.006
I'm going to shake you out of anyone's being insane.
“我要把你从任何发疯的状态中摇醒。”

00:09:54.006 --> 00:09:55.787
I'm going to snap you out of it.
“我要让你清醒过来。”

00:09:55.787 --> 00:09:58.905
I'm going to be the person that says this is what it is.
“我要做那个指出事实真相的人。”

00:09:58.905 --> 00:10:00.797
And in this one, she's just wrong.
但在这一集里，她就是错的。

00:10:00.797 --> 00:10:02.300
She has run up a huge debt.
她欠下了巨额债务。

00:10:02.300 --> 00:10:10.983
She's never told Marshall they got married with him not knowing that, I really enjoyed how much she's in the wrong in this one, because she's usually right.
她结婚时瞒着马歇尔这件事，我非常喜欢她在这一集里错得离谱的设定，因为她平时总是对的。

00:10:10.983 --> 00:10:12.097
She's usually right.
她通常都是对的。

00:10:12.097 --> 00:10:15.269
It's really interesting seeing the right person be wrong.
看那个一贯正确的人犯错真的很有意思。

00:10:15.269 --> 00:10:26.962
And the other thing we're trying to acknowledge, which I play as Josh with what you're saying, I think we were pretty honest about money and what I really are at least honest that money would be an issue to these folks.
我们要承认的另一件事是，顺着乔什你的话来说，我觉得我们在金钱方面相当诚实，或者说至少承认金钱对这些人来说是个问题。

00:10:26.962 --> 00:10:40.789
But we always talked about this in the writer's room and sometimes even people would ask us, fans would ask us, how can Lilly, a kindergarten public school teacher, afford the amazing wardrobe, that again, a wardrobe department is putting on her on a TV show.
但我们总是在编剧室里讨论这个，有时甚至粉丝也会问我们：“莉莉作为一个公立学校的幼儿园老师，怎么买得起那些惊艳的服装？”——当然，那是电视剧里的服装部门给她搭配的。

00:10:40.789 --> 00:10:41.789
And it looks like that.
而且看起来非常时髦。

00:10:41.789 --> 00:10:43.230
She got very fashionable season three.
她在第三季变得非常时尚。

00:10:43.230 --> 00:10:45.230
She's dressed very fashionably.
她穿得非常时髦。

00:10:45.230 --> 00:10:48.309
And we thought, let's acknowledge that, right?
我们就想，不如承认这一点吧？

00:10:48.309 --> 00:10:53.549
Fans of friends are always like, how can they be in that huge gigantic mansion apartment that they're in?
《老友记》的粉丝总是会问：他们怎么能住得起那么大、那么巨大的公寓？

00:10:53.549 --> 00:11:06.110
I think friends did try to explain that, but we said, this came up enough that we said, let's just do an episode where we acknowledge that no, she cannot afford all these clothes and all these bags and all these boots, she can't.
我觉得《老友记》曾试图解释过，但我们觉得这个问题被问得够多了，于是我们决定拍一集来承认：不，她根本买不起所有这些衣服、所有的包和所有的靴子，她买不起。

00:11:06.110 --> 00:11:07.509
And it's a fucking problem.
这他妈是个大问题。

00:11:07.509 --> 00:11:11.269
But also, I was reminded, don't they also have wedding debt?
不过话说回来，我突然想起来，他们是不是还有婚礼债务？

00:11:11.269 --> 00:11:12.870
Like that, it's not just the shopping debt.
就那种，不只是购物债务。

00:11:12.870 --> 00:11:16.070
I wish we'd mentioned that actually, because that doesn't just go away, right?
我真希望我们当时提到了这一点，因为那笔钱不会凭空消失，对吧？

00:11:16.070 --> 00:11:25.110
They totally had wedding debt from this dress fiasco and like Marshall got, like we made a point of that in season two and we didn't really tap it.
因为婚纱的闹剧，他们确实留下了婚礼债务，而且马歇尔——我们在第二季里强调过这一点，但之后并没有怎么深入挖掘。

00:11:25.110 --> 00:11:26.110
I wish we'd mention it.
我真希望我们当时提到了它。

00:11:26.110 --> 00:11:32.190
Let's just say that the wedding dress debt is part of the credit card debt that comes back to haunt her at the next time.
我们就当婚纱欠下的债也是信用卡债务的一部分吧，这会在下一集里继续纠缠她。

00:11:32.190 --> 00:11:36.509
I'll say it all adds up in that very clever and we didn't forget to say that.
我会说这一切在那个巧妙的设计中都积聚了起来，我们没有忘记这一点。

00:11:36.509 --> 00:11:45.679
And I wrote you this little ditty to sing to you in New York City.
我为你写了这首小曲，要在纽约市唱给你听。

00:11:45.679 --> 00:11:49.740
We'll be right back.
我们马上回来。

00:11:49.740 --> 00:11:53.500
Hi, I'm Alex Goldman, host of the Hyper-Fixed podcast.
嗨，我是艾利克斯·戈德曼，《Hyper-Fixed》播客的主持人。

00:11:53.500 --> 00:11:57.019
Each week, we take listeners' problems and try to solve them for them.
每周，我们都会倾听听众的烦恼并试着为他们解决。

00:11:57.019 --> 00:12:00.139
Problems like, I'm 30 and I'm scared to drive in New York.
比如这样的问题：“我30岁了，但不敢在纽约开车。”

00:12:00.139 --> 00:12:03.980
Or, why can't I adjust the volume of my car stereo when I'm in reverse?
或者：“为什么当我挂倒档时，不能调节汽车音响的音量？”

00:12:03.980 --> 00:12:05.836
we also solve non-car related problems.
我们也会解决与汽车无关的问题。

00:12:05.836 --> 00:12:11.740
If you have a problem, not only will we fix it, we'll expose the hidden systems that caused that problem in the first place.
如果你有什么烦恼，我们不仅会帮你解决，还会揭示导致该问题的背后隐藏机制。

00:12:12.519 --> 00:12:15.148
That's the HyperFixed Podcast from Radiotopia.
这就是来自Radiotopia的《Hyper-Fixed》播客。

00:12:15.148 --> 00:12:18.519
Find it wherever you find podcasts or at HyperFixedPod.com.
你可以在各大播客平台或访问 HyperFixedPod.com 找到它。

00:12:48.639 --> 00:12:54.259
Like you guys in this episode, you were talking about environmental devastation and porn.
就像你们在这一集里探讨的那样，你们聊到了环境破坏和色情制品。

00:12:54.259 --> 00:13:02.240
Two issues that have only swollen, if you have only gotten bigger as the years have gone on.
这两个问题随着时间的推移，只有不断膨胀，变得越来越严重。

00:13:02.240 --> 00:13:07.639
So tip of the hat to the prophetic writer's room of how I met your mother.
所以，向《老爸老妈浪漫史》富有先见之明的编剧室致敬。

00:13:07.639 --> 00:13:18.279
Yeah, and the idea of selling out the environment to corporate concerns and letting go of these ideals because you're tempted by money like that, that's in the news, that's a thing.
是的，为了企业利益出卖环境，因为抵挡不住金钱的诱惑而放弃理想，这经常出现在新闻里，是现实存在的事。

00:13:18.279 --> 00:13:19.279
It's unfortunately.
这很不幸。

00:13:19.279 --> 00:13:37.399
And it's also like, I don't know, like, there's something really tender and sweet about watching one's like youthful ideals, like not quite curdle, but just yield to real world metrics, you know?
而且这也是，怎么说呢，看着某人年少时的理想——虽然没有完全变质，但只是向现实世界的功利标准低头——这个过程有一种非常温柔而又酸楚的感觉，你知道吗？

00:13:37.399 --> 00:13:38.399
Yeah.
对。

00:13:38.399 --> 00:13:39.399
Yeah.
对。

00:13:39.399 --> 00:13:46.519
Like, Marshall, I mean, didn't you plant it in flashbacks, he was a little kid and he got like concerned about the environment, right?
就像马歇尔，我的意思是，闪回里不是演过吗？他还是个小男孩的时候就很关心环境，对吧？

00:13:46.519 --> 00:13:48.480
Yeah, yeah, life among the gorillas.
对，对，大猩猩的生活。

00:13:48.480 --> 00:13:49.559
He had life among the gorillas.
他演过《大猩猩的生活》。

00:13:49.559 --> 00:13:50.399
Exactly.
没错。

00:13:50.399 --> 00:13:53.200
He's seen good old type woman come visit his school when he was a kid.
他小时候见过亲切的简·古道尔来他的学校参观。

00:13:53.200 --> 00:13:58.080
Yeah, and he's a true believer and a real sincere guy around this stuff.
对，他是这方面的坚定信仰者，也是一个非常真诚的人。

00:13:58.080 --> 00:14:07.000
But then, you know, it's kind of like, well, I can have this little plot of land that I can grow my family on.
但随后，你知道的，就有点像：“好吧，我可以拥有这一小块土地，用来繁衍我的家庭。”

00:14:07.000 --> 00:14:08.840
And what's so wrong with that?
那又有什么错呢？

00:14:08.840 --> 00:14:13.639
I do think that you cast exactly the right actors to seduce him because John Cho.
我觉得你们确实选对了演员来诱惑他，因为约翰·赵。

00:14:13.639 --> 00:14:14.480
He's so good in this.
他在这一集里演得太好了。

00:14:14.480 --> 00:14:16.480
He's really good in this.
他在这一集里真的很棒。

00:14:16.480 --> 00:14:20.919
I tell you a John Cho related Hollywood story.
我给你们讲个关于约翰·赵的好莱坞故事。

00:14:20.919 --> 00:14:21.919
Please.
请讲。

00:14:21.919 --> 00:14:36.600
So do you remember, and I think I've talked about this guy, I've talked about this a lot because it was part of my origin story as a professional actor, my very first audition in LA, I got cast by the white's brothers and Danny Zuker in this show for the WB called Off-Center.
你们还记得吗——我想我可能说过这事，我经常提起它，因为这是我作为职业演员的起点故事——我在洛杉矶的第一次试镜，被怀特兄弟和丹尼·祖克选中，出演华纳兄弟（WB）的一部名为《基情四射》的剧。

00:14:36.600 --> 00:14:43.279
It was my first audition in LA in my first room, and I got this part, we shot the pilot.
那是我在洛杉矶的第一次试镜，进的第一个房间，然后我得到了这个角色，我们拍摄了试播集。

00:14:43.279 --> 00:14:44.279
I'm waiting.
我在等。

00:14:44.279 --> 00:14:45.279
I'm waiting.
我在等。

00:14:45.279 --> 00:14:46.279
I'm waiting.
我在等。

00:14:46.279 --> 00:14:48.120
it's gonna go, it's gonna go.
要播了，要播了。

00:14:48.120 --> 00:14:56.039
They picked up the pilot and replaced me, fired me, essentially, which is a very common story in Hollywood.
他们选了另一个试播集主演并换掉了我，基本上就是炒了我，这在好莱坞是很常见的事。

00:14:56.039 --> 00:15:01.559
It's happened to a lot of people, but in that pilot was a young John Cho.
很多人都经历过，但在那个试播集里有个年轻的约翰·赵。

00:15:01.559 --> 00:15:03.440
I forgot that, I knew where you're going with this.
我都忘了，我本来就知道你要说到这儿。

00:15:03.440 --> 00:15:04.919
I remember that pilot.
我还记得那个试播集。

00:15:04.919 --> 00:15:10.320
Yeah, so I worked with John that whole week or two and he was awesome, he was so great.
对，所以我跟约翰合作了那一整个星期或两周，他太棒了，真的非常棒。

00:15:10.320 --> 00:15:14.799
This is all pre-hearled and Kumar, like, you know.
这一切都发生在《寻堡奇遇》之前，你知道的。

00:15:14.799 --> 00:15:17.480
but it was when we were, you know, we were all on the pilot circuit together.
但那是我们都在一起跑试播集的时候。

00:15:17.480 --> 00:15:20.000
Show was like the guy off American Pie at that point.
当时那家伙就像是《美国派》里的那个演员。

00:15:20.000 --> 00:15:22.320
He had a funny little turn in American Pie.
他在《美国派》里有个很有趣的小角色。

00:15:22.320 --> 00:15:26.080
I think that was his claim to fame at that moment before all this other big shit, yeah.
我想那可以说是他在经历其他那些大火之前，当时成名的代表作吧。

00:15:26.080 --> 00:15:27.456
And they replaced me with Eddie K.
然后他们换上了埃迪·K·

00:15:27.456 --> 00:15:29.360
Thomas from American Pie, so it all came first.
托马斯，就是《美国派》里的那个，所以一切都联系上了。

00:15:29.360 --> 00:15:31.000
Yeah, yeah, yeah, see?
对，对，对，你看？

00:15:31.000 --> 00:15:32.679
The deck was stacked against you.
当时的所有牌都对你不利。

00:15:32.679 --> 00:15:34.000
No.
不是。

00:15:34.000 --> 00:15:36.519
But I mean, it all ended out to be great.
但我的意思是，结果一切都很好。

00:15:36.519 --> 00:15:46.379
Like, in a lot of ways, it was a very, how I met your mother-ish kind of thing because it was like, I wanted it to go one way and it went another way.
从很多方面来看，这很像那种《老爸老妈浪漫史》式的经历，因为就好像，我希望事情按一个方向发展，结果却去了另一个方向。

00:15:46.379 --> 00:15:48.600
And it ended out to be just the greatest thing for me.
最后证明这对我都不能再好了。

00:15:48.600 --> 00:15:54.600
One, it, well, it freed me up for some great work that came along.
第一，它，嗯，它让我腾出时间接了后来出现的一些很棒的工作。

00:15:54.600 --> 00:16:00.240
The next season I got on this John Well show with Sally Field called The Court and then I did The Graduate on Broadway.
第二季我参演了萨莉·菲尔德主演的约翰·韦尔斯剧集《法庭》，然后我在百老汇演了《毕业生》。

00:16:00.240 --> 00:16:03.320
Like, things just opened up for me after that.
就像，那之后我的机会全打开了。

00:16:03.320 --> 00:16:08.279
But it really taught me, I remember my mom saying, go back out to LA.
但这真的教会了我，我记得我妈妈说，回洛杉矶去。

00:16:08.279 --> 00:16:13.159
Like, don't act like LA shut the door on your career out there.
别表现得好像洛杉矶对你的职业生涯关上了大门一样。

00:16:13.159 --> 00:16:16.559
like go back, get a back up on the horse, you know?
就回去，重新振作起来，你知道吗？

00:16:16.559 --> 00:16:18.720
And I did, and here we are.
我照做了，然后我们就坐在这里了。

00:16:18.720 --> 00:16:20.399
But it was- I love that story.
但我——我喜欢这个故事。

00:16:20.399 --> 00:16:23.120
I never knew your mom was like giving you the pep talk.
我以前不知道你妈妈还给你过这种鼓舞。

00:16:23.120 --> 00:16:33.039
Well, she, you know, I was dating this woman at the time and she was gonna go back out there and it was kind of like, I was just hesitant because I felt like really stung, you know?
嗯，她，你知道，我当时在和一个女人交往，她要回那边去，然后就有点像，我当时很犹豫，因为我觉得真的很受打击，你知道吗？

00:16:33.039 --> 00:16:34.320
No, it's terrible feeling.
不，那种感觉太糟糕了。

00:16:34.320 --> 00:16:35.480
It is a terrible feeling.
这真的是一种糟糕的感觉。

00:16:35.480 --> 00:16:37.840
In that moment, that is a fucking terrible feeling.
在那一刻，那他妈的绝对是一种糟糕的感觉。

00:16:37.840 --> 00:16:39.159
I'm sorry you went through that.
我很遗憾你经历了那些。

00:16:39.159 --> 00:16:42.480
But I found this like new resilience.
但我发现了一种全新的韧性。

00:16:42.480 --> 00:16:44.919
Like I found this like, I could take a punch.
就像我发现，我抗击打能力挺强的。

00:16:44.919 --> 00:16:45.759
You know what I mean?
你知道我的意思吗？

00:16:45.759 --> 00:16:49.799
It is so good for young actors and young anybody listening to that show that I take a punch.
这对年轻演员和听这个节目的任何年轻人来说都太好了，我能承受挫折。

00:16:49.799 --> 00:16:54.240
I'm so glad you're talking about this because it does fucking happen.
我很高兴你谈到这一点，因为这种事他妈的确实会发生。

00:16:54.240 --> 00:16:56.039
Yeah, it happens a lot.
对，这经常发生。

00:16:56.039 --> 00:16:59.840
And your 20s are about like learning how to take a punch in certain way.
